From 055f8428fd521de48efda7bccd8c67c5196a9dae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 02:49:50 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/25] Video: Swap Eyes in the 3D Video menu, over every mark

The 3D Video menu gets Swap Eyes, a check box: each eye sees the other
eye's view, whatever decided the picture's arrangement (the stream's
frame packing SEI, the container's mark, the user's choice or, last, the
picture's shape), so a video marked the wrong way round is corrected by
its viewer. The choice is kept on the element (stereoSwap, for the
browser's own UI only; pages do not see it) and travels with each frame
to the compositor: on a DMABuf surface (SurfaceDescriptorDMABuf), with a
frame decoded in the media process (SurfaceDescriptorRemoteDecoder,
applied in the compositor through TextureHost::ApplyStereoSwap), and in
the stereo mark WebRender carries to its own surfaces (bit 9).
NativeLayerWayland swaps the eyes last (SwapStereoEyes).

YCbCr buffer textures also take the user's choice of arrangement, which
until now reached DMABuf pictures only.

A layer WebRender draws a video into now copies views in another order
or on top of each other side by side, left eye first, as an external
layer does: on the GPU (a framebuffer blit) with hardware WebRender, in
memory with software WebRender.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
